## Decisions applied (Dean, 2026-07-28)

1. **results/ — discarded.** None of the 2026-06-15 runs succeeded; raw logs/CSVs/plots not
   preserved. (The earlier commit `d60b2d94` that included 63M of results was amended away →
   `892e1efa`; the 46M+17M controller.log blobs are no longer in any reachable commit.)
2. **llm-d-benchmark clone changes — no exact patch.** The knowledge is already self-sufficient
   in the two docs (runbook §5.1/5.2/9 = chart 0.7.0/RBAC CrashLoop fix; guidellm-notes =
   HF_TOKEN 401 + guidellm-0.6.0 request-format fix + v0.6.1 pin + upstream TODO). Concrete
   samples (3 profiles + patched guide yaml) kept as local reference for re-applying against a
   clean llm-d-benchmark tip *if broken*.
3. **Two WVA harness commits (`benchmark-settings.env` + scenario-1 guide) — not cherry-picked.**
   Likely superseded by the updated benchmark code; kept as local reference files only. Still
   preserved in git on `origin/benchmark` + `benchmark-ta3-legacy` regardless.
4. **We did NOT change `llm-d` / `llm-d-infra`** — no such clone exists in this worktree.

## Zero-loss verification (unchanged from first pass)

68 local-vs-origin commits = TA/engine code merged to main + upstream PR pulls; the 2 genuine
harness commits are patch-id-identical to origin/benchmark's `11fcb418`/`013d4976`. No unpreserved
harness work in the local commits.

## What Dean must do (pushes — coder cannot). Fork (origin) only, NEVER upstream.

1. `git push origin archive/benchmark-ta3-legacy` (push the tag first).
2. `git push -u origin benchmark` — ⚠️ **rewrites `origin/benchmark`** (fresh branch = main tip;
   the 2 harness commits currently on origin/benchmark survive via the archive tag + legacy branch).
   Non-fast-forward → `--force-with-lease`; confirm intent.
3. Optionally delete local `benchmark-ta3-legacy` branch after the tag is pushed (harmless to keep).

